 line, read values on section\nstart and end lines, section terminating character, ‘/’, can appear\nanywhere on a line. All of these are ignored if the value is in ‘quotes’.', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.read_fortran_namelist', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.io.espresso.read_fortran_namelist', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.read_fortran_namelist', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'read_fortran_namelist', 'class': None, 'function': 'read_fortran_namelist', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 2}, 'score': 2.7788209915161133, 'vector_score': 0.37314993143081665, 'bm25_score': 18.266376284804803, 'rerank_score': 2.7788209915161133}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in\n\nase.io.espresso. write_espresso_in ( fd , atoms , input_data = None , pseudopotentials = None , kspacing = None , kpts = None , koffset = (0, 0, 0) , crystal_coordinates = False , additional_cards = None , ** kwargs ) [source] #\n\nCreate an input file for pw.x.\n\nUse set_initial_magnetic_moments to turn on spin, if nspin is set to 2\nwith no magnetic moments, they will all be set to 0.0. Magnetic moments\nwill be converted to the QE units (fraction of valence electrons) using\nany pseudopotential files found, or a best guess for the number of\nvalence electrons.\n\nUnits are not converted for any other input data, so use Quantum ESPRESSO\nunits (Usually Ry or atomic units).\n\nKeys with a dimension (e.g. Hubbard_U(1)) will be incorporated as-is\nso the i should be made to match the output.\n\nImplemented features:', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 